        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 1162,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T16:35:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1124,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 1163,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155852,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 1163,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>AFCMT occurs exclusively on acral sites and is about twice as common on the hands (particularly the fingers) as on the feet {32047233; 39181449}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T16:35:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1125,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 1164,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155853,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 1164,
        "headingText": "\r\n<h5>Signs and symptoms</h5>\r\n<p>Tumours present as slow-growing small soft tissue&ndash;based lesions, while rare cases have been more superficially located and involve the dermis {32047233; 39181449; 36936733; 32844242}.</p>\r\n<h5>Imaging findings</h5>\r\n<p>Plain radiographs show extrinsic cortical scalloping or mild saucerization of the underlying bone. On CT studies, AFCMT presents as a soft tissue or periosteal lesion with possible erosion of the underlying bone. MRI shows low to intermediate signal on T1-weighted images, marked hyperintense signal on T2-weighted images, and heterogeneous enhancement after intravenous contrast medium injection {32844242; 39181449}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T16:35:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1126,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 1165,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155854,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 1165,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>AFCMT has been described to occur in middle-aged adults, a recent case series reporting a median age of 44&nbsp;years and a slight female predominance {39181449}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T16:35:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1127,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 1166,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155855,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 1166,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T16:35:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1128,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 1167,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155856,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 1167,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>THBS1</em>::<em>ADGRF5</em> fusions were identified in 27&nbsp;of 29&nbsp;cases {32047233; 39181449}. <em>THBS1</em> is the 5&prime; partner and encodes a member of the non-collagenous matrix glycoproteins of the extracellular matrix. The 3&prime; partner is <em>ADGRF5</em>, which encodes an orphan transmembrane G&nbsp;protein-coupled receptor. At the transcriptional level, the tumours show major upregulation of the ADGRF5 transcript, not confirmed at the protein level.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T16:35:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1135,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 1174,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155857,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 1174,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours present as well-circumscribed tan nodules.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T16:35:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1129,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 1168,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155858,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 1168,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>AFCMT is a multinodular tumour delineated by fibrous bands with numerous small vessels. Tumour cells are spindle or round, embedded in an abundant myxoid, chondroid, or fibrous stroma. They form poorly defined groups or small clusters or rows, sometimes embedded in lacunar spaces, hinting at a cartilaginous differentiation. The neoplastic cells have scant eosinophilic cytoplasm; small round, ovoid, or reniform nuclei with occasionally longitudinal grooves reminiscent of chondroblasts; and inconspicuous nucleoli. Usually, there is no pleomorphism or mitotic activity. Cystic-like changes, foci of calcifications, or ischaemic necrosis can rarely be present. By immunohistochemistry, CD34 and ERG were positive in 94% and 97% of cases, respectively.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T16:35:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1130,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 1169,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155859,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 1169,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Insufficient data</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T16:35:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1131,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 1170,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155860,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 1170,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>THBS1</em>::<em>ADGRF5</em> fusion or rearrangement of <em>THBS1</em> supports the diagnosis but is generally not required in a morphological typical case.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T16:35:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1134,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 1173,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155861,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 1173,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> multinodular tumour with fibrous, myxoid, or chondroid stroma, fibrovascular septa, spindle or round bland cells; acral locations.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> CD34 and ERG expression; <em>THBS1</em>::<em>ADGRF5</em> fusion in select cases.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T16:35:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1132,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 1171,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155862,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 1171,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not applicable</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T16:35:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1133,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 1172,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 155863,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 1172,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours behave indolently, with some risk of local recurrence (~18%) if incompletely excised. No reports of malignant transformation or distant metastasis exist to date {32047233; 39181449}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T16:35:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]